198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (The metaball function in Grasshopper is a strong tool for creating organic, blob-like 2D curves from a series of input points and their charge values. It uses a field summation technique to generate smooth, continuous shapes that blend and merge as the points become closer together. The function creates these curves by sampling the space around each point, computing elevations using a fall-off equation, and intersecting the resulting landscape with a horizontal plane at a given iso-surface value. This approach enables designers to build complex, flowing geometries suitable for a wide range of parametric design applications, including architectural forms and digital art. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
