212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Voronoi diagrams in Grasshopper provide an effective method for creating cellular patterns inspired by nature. Voronoi component requires points, a boundary, and a plane as inputs.  To generate points, we use the Populate 2D component, which makes random points within a defined boundary. The resulting Voronoi diagram will display in the Rhino viewport, dividing the space into cells, each containing the area closest to the central point. This basic arrangement allows for easy experimentation with various patterns and forms, making it a useful tool for developing intricate, nature-inspired structures.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
