249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Physarealm is a multi-objective system as a Grasshopper plugin that was inspired by the behaviour of Physarum polycephalum, a slime mould. Ma Yidong created this open-source application, which simulates the development, growth, and minimisation of transportation networks using stigmergy techniques similar to ant colony optimisation. Physarealm enables us to create sophisticated, organic-looking structures in 3D, expanding upon the initial 2D implementations. The plugin supports artistic expression and may simulate slime mould behaviour on meshes. Physarealm's agent-based system uses simple individual behaviours to mimic the biological behaviour of Physarum, making it a powerful tool for investigating bio-inspired design ideas within the Grasshopper environment. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
